01:00:51,818 --> 01:00:57,818
Beverly Hills Cop II is a 1987 American buddy cop action comedy film directed by Tony
Scott, written by Larry Ferguson and Warren Skaaren, and starring Eddie Murphy.

14
01:05:32,727 --> 01:05:38,727
It is the sequel to the 1984 film Beverly Hills Cop and the second
installment in the Beverly Hills Cop film series.

15
01:10:13,636 --> 01:10:19,636
Murphy returns as Detroit police detective Axel Foley, who reunites with Beverly Hills detectives Billy Rosewood (Judge Reinhold) and John
Taggart (John Ashton) to stop a criminal organization after Captain Andrew Bogomil (Ronny Cox) is shot and seriously wounded.

16
01:14:54,545 --> 01:15:00,545
The film was released on May 20, 1987, by Paramount Pictures.

17
01:19:35,454 --> 01:19:41,454
It received mixed reviews from critics on release, but it was a box
office success, grossing $300 million worldwide.

18
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:22,363
Additionally, the film was nominated for an Oscar, as well as a Golden Globe
Award for Best Original Song, for Bob Seger's "Shakedown".

19
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:03,272
Two sequels, Beverly Hills Cop III and Beverly Hills Cop:
Axel F, were released in 1994 and 2024.

20
01:33:38,181 --> 01:33:44,181
The film explores themes of police, arms smuggling,
intensive care, undercover, detective.

21
01:38:19,090 --> 01:38:25,090
The tone is lighthearted.
